Z||000000||Stan86SE||04-16-2001||12:01 PM||||My apologies for asking a question that I'm *sure* has been asked a couple zillion times, but this is my first time doing this and I want be sure I (hopefully) know what I'm doing before I get started.  (2.8L, V6)<P>I'm gonna replace the pickup coil and distributor O ring.  I know to mark the orientation of the base and also the position of the rotor before I pull the distributor.  My tired old question is: For correct timing, when I put the distributor back in, I orient the rotor to the position it stopped at when I 'pulled' the distributor, right? (not its original position)  Is this right?<P>Hope I made sense and thanks for any help!<P>- Stan  <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-16-2001||12:41 PM||||Sounds Good!<BR>If you marked both positions (in and out) and install in reverse order, it will drop baack into place correctly. Then line up your bottom mark and your all set.||||reg||1
